etres (240,000 sq mi). As of 2024, it has a population of 5,357,744, consisting of about 80 ethnic groups. Having been a French colony under the name Ubangi-Shari, French is its official language, with Sango, a Ngbandi-based creole language, as the national and co-official language. Its capital and largest city is Bangui, which sits on the country's southern border with the Democratic Republic of the Congo.","description":"Country in Central Africa","thumbnailUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Flag_of_the_Central_African_Republic.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_Central_African_Republic.svg.png","canonicalUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_African_Republic","revisionTimestamp":"2026-07-30T09:14:38Z"}},"trade":{"ok":false,"reason":"Comtrade HTTP 429 for reporter 140 flow M"},"weather":{"ok":true,"data":{"temperatureC":24.4,"windKph":10.1,"observedAt":"2026-08-02T20:15"}},"fx":{"ok":false,"reason":"XAF not covered by Frankfurter"},"famousPeople":{"ok":true,"data":[]},"overrides":{},"capturedAt":"2026-08-02T20:18:22.492Z"}